KZ3 patch 1164: EDAT reader seeks and reads the cache size with 64 bits.

edat_decrypt_file seeked with fseek(in, (long)offset): a long is 32 bits on Windows, so the first block past 2 GiB failed
(rc -9, half-written cache removed). Fix: edat_seek (_fseeki64 / fseeko) for both seeks. KZ3's packs are probably below
2 GiB (ASSUMPTION), so no KZ3 gain is expected; for large DLC/EDATs and as an upstream candidate. Not in this patch:
edat_cache_valid's st_size compare (vekta 4016, 32-bit _off_t on MinGW): that function comes from patch 5002, which sorts
after 1xxx, so the one-line change (a 64-bit size compare there) is still to be made in that patch. Test:
tools/spu/test_vekta_helpers.sh (sparse 3 GiB file, marker at 2.5 GiB) with a negative control.
